{"availability":"available","full":"muchimi/JoystickGremlinEx","name":"JoystickGremlinEx","description":"Modified version of Joystick Gremlin to add features I wanted to have but were difficult to do as just a plugin, plus I wanted to run this as 64 bit and on a more current version of Python/QT.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":129,"forks":18,"created":"2023-03-01T17:28:30Z","updated":"2026-10-08T15:13:13Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"develop","homepage":"https://muchimi.github.io/JoystickGremlinEx/","topics":["advanced-macro","hardware-cockpit","joystick","joystick-remote-control","midi","msfs","osc","simconnect","simulation-control","star-citizen","vjoy"],"demo":"https://muchimi.github.io/JoystickGremlinEx/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:16.108Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:16.108Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:16.108Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:53:31.089Z","stars":129,"forks":18},{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:16.108Z","stars":129,"forks":18}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["GremlinEx (GEX) is a universal controller integrator: it allows you to take input from multiple hardware devices from different manufacturers connected to a local machine, or a remote machine, such as joysticks and HID controllers, OSC (Open Sound Control), MIDI, Keyboard and mouse inputs and map them to virtual outputs like VJOY, or keyboard or mouse output, convert text to speech and play sounds. It can send output to a game or another process.","With OSC support, GremlinEx can receive input from custom designed glass (touch screen) surfaces, and supports two way communication to any device supported by BitFocus Companion such as the Elgato Streamdeck. This communication is two-way so GremlinEx can also send data to a glass surface or an external hardware panel.","GremlinEx can be expanded using custom plugins written in Python."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com